      "id": "N1_post_no_overflow_native",
      "desc": "0cdada0 fieldRow/fieldCell: no cell overflows the card content box on Yoga, 4 widths x 4 scales",
      "pass": true,
      "detail": "16/16 clean (max overflow 0px; cells are flex-sized, so the 13pt text scaling to AX5 cannot widen the box)"
    },
    {
      "id": "N2_pre_also_clean_native_web_only_bug",
      "desc": "b40b742 flex:1 row: ALSO no overflow on Yoga -> defect 1 was web-only, native never shipped it",
      "pass": true,
      "detail": "16/16 clean; Yoga's default minWidth is undefined and a flexBasis-sized node never measures content width, so there is no intrinsic floor to overflow"
    },
    {
      "id": "W4_control_css_minwidth_reproduces_bug",
      "desc": "control: pre-fix styles + emulated CSS min-width:auto overflow on phone widths (validates the engine model)",
      "pass": true,
      "detail": "12/12 phone cases overflow once the intrinsic floor is restored (e.g. 320pt/L-default: floor 165px/cell vs 254px box -> +86px)"
    },
    {
      "id": "C3_wrap_parity_web_vs_native",
      "desc": "post-fix wrap decision is identical on Yoga and on react-native-web at every width",
      "pass": true,
      "detail": "320pt: 1->2 line(s), 360pt: 1->2 line(s), 390pt: 1->2 line(s), 1440pt: 1->1 line(s) — matches web sameRow exactly, so the two platforms stack and unstack together"
    },
    {
      "id": "C3b_native_layout_delta_is_a_visual_change",
      "desc": "the native delta is reported, not silently passed: cells that were side-by-side now stack below 410px of content box",
      "pass": true,
      "detail": "320pt (254px box < 410px), 360pt (294px box < 410px), 390pt (324px box < 410px) stack on native where they previously sat side-by-side; 1440pt (1374px box) is unchanged at 1 line. Native had no overflow to fix, so this is a pure visual change there — intentional and consistent with web, but it is a native-visible delta the web-only harness could not see."
    }
  ],
